<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean plantings 52 percent done - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean plantings 52 percent done - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian soybean plantings were 52 percent completed by November 21 against 54 percent by November 23, 1995 and an average of the past five years of 52 percent, consultants Safras e Mercado said.</p>
<p>The pace of plantings had slowed in the past week due to rains throughout almost all the growing region, Safras said in its weekly report.</p>
<p>Given however the recommended planting period is until December 15, there are no concerns over productivity at this stage, it added.</p>
</text>
